  "source": { "doc": "mk70.pdf", "page": "7 to 9", "section": "Ordering Schematic" },
  "note": "Extracted by hand from the ordering schematic. Nine models on one sheet, the standard, equal percentage and linear characteristics each plain or with a side or top positioner. The Cv column is split by model, and the shared digits mean different flows on each side, so the labels carry both readings and the exclusive codes refuse the other family. The range and actuator position is the sheet's own six character code; the two printed tables are carried whole, with the narrower Mark 70 Series header on the first pair noted for John rather than turned into a constraint. The handwheel and I/P accessories name their actuator in their own labels, so they refuse a system from another actuator class. The end connection glosses couple body and size exactly as printed, IFE for ductile iron above 2 inch or carbon or stainless, FE for ductile iron below 2-1/2 inch or bronze.",
